From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 11:52:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] codegen: use non-committing deployment analysis

Route standalone codegen through evaluate_push with an explicit analysis request instead of beginning the start_push deployment lifecycle. Refuse older backend responses without analysis rather than falling back to a request that can publish pending schema and index metadata.

Keep dev and deploy on start_push, omit the analysis request from deployment preflight, and preserve compatibility with legacy evaluation responses for a precise version error. Generate API, data-model, component, and environment types from a narrow shared analysis contract and fail clearly when component analysis is incomplete.

Add response-decoder coverage, operator patch guidance, and an Unreleased changelog entry.
